From: Uri Goldshtein <uri.goldshtein@gmail.com>
Date: Sun, 11 Oct 2026 09:27:29 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] Export from the terminal without the extension: npm run
 export

A member who wants their records on a schedule, or without installing
anything, runs the collector from Node. scripts/headless-export.mjs opens
the browser and signs in as scripts/live-run.mjs does (that part moves to
scripts/maccabi-browser.mjs, shared by both), bundles src/core/ with Vite
into dist-cli/ through src/cli/index.ts, and runs the steps with two seams
of its own (scripts/headless-lib.mjs): the Maccabi Online page as the
Transport, with every request evaluated inside the page as the extension
sends them from the tab, and a folder as the Sink, with the extension's
write rules and a content index so a rerun asks for no document it has.
The folder gets the same root files as a ZIP, README.md included.

Test results by default, --all for every section, --steps for some. It
never orders the medical file, so nothing on the account changes and
Maccabi sends no SMS. test/headless.test.ts runs the test-results step
through both seams against the fake site, with the in-page sources
evaluated for real.

